BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Talk featuring Sally Hayden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261026T190000
UID:bm-6432020261026@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/7600763/Website2/
 Events/10_26_26.png?cb=1790270254
DESCRIPTION:[at Ben McNally Books]\nJoin us at Ben McNally Books for a spe
 cial evening with journalist Sally Hayden\, former winner of the Irish Boo
 k of the Year (\nMy Fourth Time\, We Drowned\n)\, and author of\nThis is A
 lso a Love Story: A Reporter's Search for Goodness in a Cruel World\n.\nSa
 lly with be joined in conversation by journalist Katie Engelhart.\nOrder 
 a copy of\nThis is Also a Love Story\nhere.\nAbout the Book\nAn acclaimed 
 reporter takes us on an unforgettable journey\, capturing the human capaci
 ty for love and connection against all odds.\nWe live in an era defined by
  crisis—whether it be war and displacement\, climate collapse\, or growi
 ng inequality\, and how the powerful profit from violence and exploitation
 . Celebrated foreign correspondent Sally Hayden has spent her career on th
 e frontlines\, uncovering some of the darkest moments of our time. Yet eve
 n in the face of unimaginable adversity\, she’s witnessed the incredible
  goodness of regular people.\nIn\nThis Is Also a Love Story\n\, Hayden ree
 xamines catastrophe through the love stories she has come across. She intr
 oduces us to a mother in northeast Nigeria who risks everything to save he
 r daughter from forced marriage to Boko Haram militants\, and to a group o
 f Syrian women who have tirelessly searched for their missing spouses and 
 children\, while launching a call for justice. We meet a couple separated 
 by the Russian invasion of Ukraine and read letters from the bereaved to t
 he dead\, still being written over a decade after the tsunami that devasta
 ted Japan. Through these stories\, which crisscross the globe\, from Ugand
 a to Lebanon\, Ghana\, Rwanda and Iraq\, she challenges us to reconsider w
 hat it means to be alive on this planet today.\nWhat if news was recounted
  through the prism of the actions and decisions people take for those they
  love? Would it become harder to dehumanize those who seem different to us
 ?\nThis Is Also a Love Story\ndares us to recognize how innate generosity 
 and self-sacrifice can be found in even the most difficult of times\, and
 —as a result—to question what might be needed to create a better world
 .\nAbout the Author\nSally Hayden is an Irish journalist focused on migrat
 ion\, conflict\, and humanitarian crises. Sally’s work has been featured
  by\nThe New York Times\, the Irish Times\, The Washington Post\, Financia
 l Times\, The Guardian\, CNN International\, Al Jazeera\, Time\, BBC\n\, a
 nd other outlets across the world. Sally’s first book\nMy Fourth Time\, 
 We Drowned\nwas the winner of the Orwell Prize and the Irish Book of the Y
 ear\, and was a finalist for the Baillie Gifford Prize and the New York Pu
 blic Library’s Helene Bernstein Book Award for excellence in journalism.
LOCATION:Ben McNally Books
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:October Social: Characters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261030T193000
UID:bm-6458020261030@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
DESCRIPTION:[Ben McNally Books Social]\nJoin us for our third social!\nThi
 s time around we'll be introducing themes to our gatherings\, and for Octo
 ber our theme will be Characters!\nAnd\, since we'll be gathering so close
  to Halloween\, we invite everyone who is brave enough to come dressed as 
 their favourite literary character! We'll have special prizes for everyone
  who comes in costume.\nCome join us to meet with fellow booklovers\, and 
 to talk to them (and us) about your favourite literary characters.\nWe'll 
 have some nibbles and some drinkies\, and we invite you to come join the f
 estivities.\nWe'll do a bit of a presentation to talk about some our own f
 avourite characters\, we'll share some news\, as well as some upcoming pla
 ns for the shop.\nBut\, more than anything\, we wanted to create a space f
 or people to mingle and socialize and get to know fellow booklovers.
LOCATION:Ben McNally Books
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Talk featuring Dan Jones
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T200000
UID:bm-6606520261110@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/7600763/Website2/
 Events/Dan_Jones_Event_blue.png?cb=1792432516
DESCRIPTION:[at Church of the Holy Trinity]\nJoin Ben McNally Books\, in p
 artnership with Penguin Canada\, for a special conversation with bestselli
 ng historian\, novelist\, and podcaster Dan Jones.\nDan will be discussing
  his new book\nCastles: A Fortified History of the World\n.\nDoors will op
 en at 6 p.m.\, the conversation will begin at 6:30. An audience Q & A will
  follow\, and Dan will be happy to sign copies of his book at the end of t
 he evening.\nTwo ticket options are available: General admission\, and Boo
 k + Ticket. Book + Ticket includes a copy of Dan Jones' latest history\,\n
 Castles: A Fortified History of the World.\nPlease note:\nneither ticket o
 ption will require a physical ticket\, and you will not be charged for del
 ivery if you choose any of the delivery options.\nAbout the Book\nFrom New
  York Times bestselling historian Dan Jones\, a grand and sweeping history
  of the world\, told through over three thousand years of iconic fortifica
 tions.\nCastles have been built to defend humanity for millennia—from th
 e walls of Troy in the Bronze Age and the desert bastion of Krak des Cheva
 liers in Syria\; to Windsor Castle and the Tower of London\; to Himeji in 
 Japan and Fort Sumter in Charleston\, South Carolina. They have inspired t
 error and passion\, foiled conquering forces\, and been deployed as the ul
 timate expression of wealth\, status\, and supremacy.\nIn\nCastles\n\, Jon
 es leads readers on a journey through the many eras of castle-building and
  across continents as each stronghold tells a unique story of power\, poli
 tics\, and survival\, revealing the shifting tides of warfare\, the rise a
 nd fall of empires\, the resilience of people under siege\, and the flouri
 shing of new ideas.\nBlending rich storytelling\, deep research\, and beau
 tiful original illustrations\,\nCastles\nis an epic story of why humans bu
 ild fortifications and how they powerfully capture our imagination. With J
 ones's trademark scholarship and flair\, he shows how defiance\, endurance
 \, and ambition have been carved into the landscapes we've inherited.\nAbo
 ut the Author\nDan Jones is the\nNew York Times\nbestselling author of\nHe
 nry V\n\,\nPowers and Thrones\n\,\nCrusaders\n\,\nThe Templars\n\,\nThe Pl
 antagenets\n\,\nWars of the Roses\n\, and\nMagna Carta\n\, as well as the\
 nEssex Dogs\ntrilogy of novels.\nHe is the host of the podcast\nThis Is Hi
 story: A Dynasty to Die For\nand has produced\, written\, and presented do
 zens of TV shows\, including the popular Netflix series Secrets of\nGreat 
 British Castles\n. As of 2025\, he is a member of the board of trustees of
  Historic Royal Palaces\, an organization dedicated to managing and mainta
 ining the unoccupied palaces of England.\nAbout the Venue\nThe Church of t
 he Holy Trinity is an Anglican Church dedicated to inclusivity and welcome
 .\nYou can learn more about the church and their mission here.\nThe church
  is located at 19 Trinity Square\, which is just behind the Toronto Eaton 
 Centre\, and accessible via University Ave.\, or else through the mall.\nY
 ou can find a map and further directions here.\nThe event will take place 
 in building #19\, and the main doors\, which face towards University Ave.\
 , will be used for entry.
LOCATION:Church of the Holy Trinity
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:45 Books in 45 Minutes\, Winter 2026 Edition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T193000
UID:bm-6576620261125@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/7600763/Website2/
 Events/2026_W45.png?cb=1791993349
DESCRIPTION:[Online Presentation]\nA contingent of McNallys will be blazin
 g through a selection of 45 (or so) new releases of the season in (about) 
 45 minutes.\nIt's the perfect opportunity to find some books for everyone 
 on your list. And\, better yet\, if you're really careful\, you can read i
 t first before you give it away. We won't tell anyone!\nThe important thin
 g is that we'll be going over some history\, biography\, thrillers\, movin
 g fiction\, and various non-fiction. Just enough to give you a taste of th
 e multitude of good books that are out there.\nFor those of you who aren't
  able to tune in on the day\, we'll have a recording available for about a
  month afterwards for those who have purchased a ticket.\nPlease note: thi
 s is for the online event! The tickets say 'in store' as a way to denote b
 eing 'in stock.' It's also worth mentioning that you can chose 'pick up' o
 r 'ship.' Either way\, since there is no physical ticket\, we will neither
  charge you for shipping nor require you to pick one up. We'll simply emai
 l you a confirmation and sign you up for the Zoom session.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
